<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bandua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bandua was a god of the pre-Roman peoples of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, worshipped in what is now northern and central Portugal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. He is known from dozens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> altar inscriptions of the Roman period, where his name often carries an epithet linking him to a particular community. He is usually seen as a protector of communities and warriors among the Callaeci and Lusitanians.</p></div>
